MiniMic Streamer nRF5340 DK 0.1.11 -- single Nucleus 7 pairing attempt
PUBLIC COPY: receiver serial replaced by ASCII 0000000000 in each 32-byte payload.
RX payload bytes 12..21 and TX payload bytes 6..15 are the only changed packet fields.
Register snapshots, radio addresses, timestamps, channels and counters are unchanged.
The unmodified original is retained locally and is not committed to Git.

Receiver was OFF before the attempt, then restarted and left off-head beside the DK.
The first valid beacon arrived 12.035646 seconds before the 30-second deadline.
Settings stayed fixed: legacy ShockBurst (no PCF), 2 Mbps, 0 dBm, 5800 us TXEN delay.
Result: 42 received beacons, 42 completed replies, no confirmation (byte 3 = 0x16).
No trace drops, CRC errors or radio faults. Pairing timed out.

READY/ADDRESS/END are hardware DPPI captures into network TIMER0 (microseconds).
TX start is READY -> START, not the earlier CPU TXEN task. These are internal RADIO
hardware events, not external RF measurements. Register snapshots are taken after
END before reconfiguration. RX logs every completed addressed packet, including
bad CRC and every byte-3 value, on the currently tuned channel and receive address.
addr_spi is nRF24 register order; addr_air lists bytes first to last on air.
TX END means local completion, not receiver acceptance.

